an general notarizations because the work is more specialized and operationally demanding."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I start as a general notary and become a loan signing agent later?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. That is a very common path. Many people start by learning general notary work, building confidence, and then adding loan signing services once they are ready."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is a loan signing agent better than being a notary public?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not automatically. It is usually better for people who want higher-ticket work and are willing to handle printers, scan-backs, deadlines, and more complex appointments. A general notary path can still be a great fit depending on your goals."}}]}]0:{"buildId":"IfVQDwM8xq3YOyshU5LTE","rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"min-h-screen bg-white","children":[["$","header",null,{"className":"border-b-4 border-notary-gold bg-notary-navy text-white","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 py-6","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-6 flex flex-col gap-4 border-b border-white/10 pb-5 md:flex-row md:items-center md:justify-between","children":[["$","$L2",null,{"href":"/","className":"text-lg font-bold tracking-[0.18em] text-white transition hover:text-notary-gold","children":"THE BEARDED NOTARY"}],["$","$L3",null,{"light":true}]]}],["$","$L2",null,{"href":"/","className":"mb-3 inline-block text-sm font-semibold text-notary-gold transition hover:text-white","children":"Back to Home"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-2 text-sm text-gray-300","children":"Updated July 2026"}],["$","h1",null,{"className":"max-w-4xl text-4xl font-bold md:text-5xl","children":"Notary Public vs. Loan Signing Agent: What Is the Difference?"}]]}]}],["$","article",null,{"className":"max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-12","children":[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$4"}}],"$L5"]}]]